esenting the Minister for Aged Care is required to attend the Senate at 9.30 am on Wednesday, 20 June 2018 to explain:* >> *(a) when the Minister first knew that the answer provided in question time on 9 May 2018, relating to home care aged packages, was incorrect; and* >> *(b) why the Minister failed to attend the chamber at the first available opportunity to correct the record.* > *(2) Any senator may move a motion to take note of the Minister's statement, and any such motion may be debated for no longer than 1 hour, and have precedence over all government business until determined.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-5226","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2018-06-19/2"}
